      "instance_name": "misogynous_framing",
      "label": "Misogynous Framing",
      "description": "The meme uses the image of a physically injured woman to justify or explain the demand for equal rights, which can be interpreted as misogynous. It reduces the complex, systemic issue of gender inequality to individual victimhood and trauma, potentially reinforcing harmful stereotypes about women as inherently vulnerable or in need of protection. This framing risks portraying women's rights activism as a reaction to personal violence rather than a broader social and political movement.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
